+// arc_sidebar_surface.h): the whole row picks up, a floating card with the
+// full card shadow follows the pointer by its grab point wherever it goes,
+// the other rows glide aside (200ms) as the pointer crosses their centres,
+// leaving the sheet closes the hole and a release there is a cancel, and
+// the card glides into its slot -- or home -- over 140ms. The transport is
+// not the pinned rows' though: this is the row's own press / drag / release,
+// not a views DnD session -- nothing leaves this list, and the OS session's
+// ESC-vs-release ambiguity on macOS is not wanted here. The card is a second
+// Row outside the ScrollView (whose viewport layer would clip it and its
